  "body": "## What changed\n\nSlice 3 of #661: the existing tool-kind glyphs (`tool-*`, from `tool_icons.rs`) now show on\n\n- the Tool library catalog rows (`pages.rs`, `tool_page`), one glyph at 16 px before each row's unchanged label;\n- the operation page's tool picker dropdown (`op_page.rs`), where `tool_icons::tool_combo` puts each document tool's glyph in front of its name (the selected-tool glyph beside the combo stays).\n\nNo new icon, no changed icon, no snapshot PNG. Item and row labels are unchanged, so accessible names do not move. The mapping is in two pure functions (`catalog_row_icon`, `picker_item_icon`) that the draw code calls and the tests pin.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `every_catalog_row_wears_its_kind_glyph` (crates/ui, `egui_app::tests::tool_icon_wiring`): every shipped catalog row's kind is a kind the editor numbers, and each row's glyph is `tool_icon(kind)`; driven from `every_tool_kind()`.\n- `every_picker_item_wears_its_kind_glyph`: for each kind, a picker item of that kind wears `tool_icon(kind)`; no tool wears nothing.\n\nBoth passed when run by name. Quick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: green on the first run (ui lib unit tests plus the boundary and theme_files suites, 3.1 min).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Nothing was looked at on screen; the glyphs' placement in the catalog row and the combo popup is untested by eye.\n- `named_glyph` (the picker's selected-tool glyph and the setup tool list) does the world lookup, which no headless test here drives; the pinned part is the pure choice.\n- No pixel snapshot covers these rows.\n\n## Owed on #661 (Refs, issue stays open)\n\nSection 5 workspace tabs (waits on paused #659) and the redraw pass after the maintainer has seen the set in the app.\n\nChangelog: Tool library rows and the operation page's tool picker show each tool kind's icon beside its name. (#661)\n\nRefs #661\n",
